1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,008
What's today's video about? A Day in the Life of an International Student.

2
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Hometown Memories and New Beginnings

3
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:16,808
It never snows in my hometown.

4
00:00:16,830 --> 00:00:21,864
The blue ocean is always in sight.

5
00:00:21,887 --> 00:00:27,387
I grew up in that warm, sunny town.

6
00:00:27,410 --> 00:00:31,797
I love cameras.

7
00:00:31,821 --> 00:00:36,581
I want to see landscapes I've never seen before.

8
00:00:36,604 --> 00:00:41,512
That's why I came to a university in Japan.

9
00:00:41,535 --> 00:00:47,369
My name is a bit long.

10
00:00:47,392 --> 00:00:54,225
But my Japanese friends call me by a cute nickname.

11
00:00:54,248 --> 00:00:58,948
I'm someone who laughs a lot.

12
00:00:58,971 --> 00:01:04,205
I love trying new things and having fun.

13
00:01:04,228 --> 00:01:09,461
Every day in Japan sparkles with excitement.

14
00:01:09,484 --> 00:01:13,519
Oh, good morning!

15
00:01:13,543 --> 00:01:17,843
Oh, Sakura! Good morning!

16
00:01:17,866 --> 00:01:21,141
You're early again today.

17
00:01:21,164 --> 00:01:25,998
Yeah, I love the morning air.

18
00:01:26,021 --> 00:01:29,961
Your camera looks cool today too.

19
00:01:29,985 --> 00:01:35,418
Yeah, it's my most treasured possession.

20
00:01:35,441 --> 00:01:39,479
What were you filming this early in the morning?

21
00:01:39,502 --> 00:01:44,661
There were little flowers blooming by the roadside.

22
00:01:44,685 --> 00:01:48,785
Not cherry blossoms, huh?

23
00:01:48,808 --> 00:01:53,241
No, they were tiny white flowers.

24
00:01:53,264 --> 00:01:56,531
They were so pretty.

25
00:01:56,554 --> 00:01:59,352
I see.

26
00:01:59,376 --> 00:02:02,242
Did you get a good shot?

27
00:02:02,265 --> 00:02:06,500
Yeah, I'll show you later.

28
00:02:06,524 --> 00:02:09,957
I can't wait!

29
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:13,364
Have you gotten used to life in Japan yet?

30
00:02:13,388 --> 00:02:17,769
Yeah, I'm starting to adjust.

31
00:02:17,793 --> 00:02:21,228
How do you like Japanese food?

32
00:02:21,251 --> 00:02:25,084
It's delicious!

33
00:02:25,107 --> 00:02:29,007
I especially love ramen.

34
00:02:29,030 --> 00:02:32,025
Ramen is so good, right?

35
00:02:32,049 --> 00:02:35,392
Which shop did you go to?

36
00:02:35,416 --> 00:02:40,249
The one in front of the station with the red sign.

37
00:02:40,272 --> 00:02:44,039
Oh, that place!

38
00:02:44,062 --> 00:02:46,861
That shop is really famous.

39
00:02:46,884 --> 00:02:51,617
Yeah, there's always a line.

40
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:54,987
Is there anything else you're struggling with?

41
00:02:55,011 --> 00:03:01,244
Hmm, studying kanji is a bit tough.

42
00:03:01,267 --> 00:03:04,236
Kanji is tricky, isn't it?

43
00:03:04,259 --> 00:03:08,093
Even Japanese people find it challenging.

44
00:03:08,116 --> 00:03:10,273
Really?

45
00:03:10,297 --> 00:03:13,663
That makes me feel a little better.

46
00:03:13,686 --> 00:03:19,153
If you ever have any questions, just ask me anytime.

47
00:03:19,176 --> 00:03:21,363
Thank you so much.

48
00:03:21,386 --> 00:03:24,653
That makes me really happy.

49
00:03:24,676 --> 00:03:27,833
Are you using a dictionary?

50
00:03:27,856 --> 00:03:32,690
Yes, I use a dictionary app on my smartphone.

51
00:03:32,713 --> 00:03:36,016
It's so convenient, right?

52
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:42,239
Yeah, but it's hard to write it yourself.

53
00:03:42,262 --> 00:03:46,296
You'll be fine if you write a little every day.

54
00:03:46,319 --> 00:03:49,630
Okay, I'll do my best!

55
00:03:49,654 --> 00:03:53,355
What's first period today?

56
00:03:53,378 --> 00:03:56,717
Japanese history.

57
00:03:56,740 --> 00:04:00,640
Oh, same as me!

58
00:04:00,664 --> 00:04:03,018
Let's go together.

59
00:04:03,041 --> 00:04:06,308
Sure, let's go!

60
00:04:06,331 --> 00:04:10,464
Is the teacher's lecture too fast to follow?

61
00:04:10,487 --> 00:04:14,228
Sometimes I don't understand.

62
00:04:14,251 --> 00:04:17,718
I'll lend you my notes, just let me know.

63
00:04:17,741 --> 00:04:22,008
Sakura, you're always so kind.

64
00:04:22,031 --> 00:04:27,387
Talking to her warms my heart.

65
00:04:27,410 --> 00:04:33,344
College life in Japan is so much fun!

66
00:04:33,367 --> 00:04:42,376
You can download today's video script from the description and top comment. Don't forget to leave a comment before downloading!

67
00:04:42,376 --> 00:04:43,876
Scene 2: Libraries and History

68
00:04:43,876 --> 00:04:47,451
Class is over.

69
00:04:47,474 --> 00:04:51,974
The university library is huge!

70
00:04:51,997 --> 00:04:57,230
There are way more books here than in my country's libraries.

71
00:04:57,254 --> 00:05:01,155
It smells like old paper.

72
00:05:01,178 --> 00:05:06,169
I love this quiet place.

73
00:05:06,193 --> 00:05:09,693
I love history.

74
00:05:09,716 --> 00:05:16,849
People in the past laughed and cried just like we do.

75
00:05:16,873 --> 00:05:21,668
It's such a strange feeling when I think about it.

76
00:05:21,692 --> 00:05:24,825
Good work today!

77
00:05:24,848 --> 00:05:29,205
Oh, Sakura! Good work!

78
00:05:29,229 --> 00:05:33,411
How was Japanese history class?

79
00:05:33,434 --> 00:05:36,734
It was really interesting!

80
00:05:36,757 --> 00:05:39,303
Seriously?

81
00:05:39,327 --> 00:05:42,110
Wasn't it difficult?

82
00:05:42,133 --> 00:05:45,927
It was a little tough.

83
00:05:45,951 --> 00:05:50,148
But the teacher's lectures are fun.

84
00:05:50,171 --> 00:05:54,938
Are you interested in old Japanese buildings?

85
00:05:54,962 --> 00:05:59,729
Yes! I love photos of temples and shrines.

86
00:05:59,752 --> 00:06:03,985
You should visit Kyoto sometime.

87
00:06:04,008 --> 00:06:06,792
Kyoto?

88
00:06:06,816 --> 00:06:09,386
Is it far?

89
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:13,795
It takes a while by Shinkansen.

90
00:06:13,819 --> 00:06:19,085
I see. I definitely want to go someday!

91
00:06:19,108 --> 00:06:22,742
There are so many historic buildings there.

92
00:06:22,765 --> 00:06:26,317
I want to take lots of photos!

93
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:29,640
The temple gardens are beautiful too.

94
00:06:29,663 --> 00:06:34,644
Japanese gardens have such beautiful trees and stones.

95
00:06:34,668 --> 00:06:39,801
Yeah, the scenery changes with the seasons.

96
00:06:39,824 --> 00:06:42,539
That sounds wonderful.

97
00:06:42,563 --> 00:06:47,030
We still have time before the next class.

98
00:06:47,053 --> 00:06:51,286
Yeah, I'll read a little.

99
00:06:51,309 --> 00:06:54,176
What are you reading?

100
00:06:54,199 --> 00:06:57,268
A Japanese manga.

101
00:06:57,291 --> 00:07:00,444
It's great for practicing kanji.

102
00:07:00,467 --> 00:07:04,567
Wait, you're studying with manga?

103
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:08,747
Yeah, the language feels so natural.

104
00:07:08,771 --> 00:07:12,346
That's cool. Good for you!

105
00:07:12,370 --> 00:07:16,703
Nah, I just really love manga.

106
00:07:16,726 --> 00:07:19,859
Got any manga recommendations?

107
00:07:19,882 --> 00:07:24,027
This sports manga is really good!

108
00:07:24,050 --> 00:07:27,398
Maybe I'll give it a read.

109
00:07:27,422 --> 00:07:31,555
You should! I can lend it to you.

110
00:07:31,578 --> 00:07:34,330
Really? Can I borrow it?

111
00:07:34,354 --> 00:07:36,496
Thanks!

112
00:07:36,519 --> 00:07:42,352
I love sharing my favorite things with friends.

113
00:07:42,375 --> 00:07:46,875
I’d love to talk more about Japanese manga too.

114
00:07:46,898 --> 00:07:54,003
The link to review today’s video is in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

115
00:07:54,003 --> 00:07:55,503
Scene 3: The Joys of a University Cafeteria

116
00:07:55,503 --> 00:07:58,936
It's lunchtime.

117
00:07:58,959 --> 00:08:03,899
The cafeteria smells amazing.

118
00:08:03,923 --> 00:08:07,023
I'm starving.

119
00:08:07,046 --> 00:08:12,683
We don’t have big cafeterias like this in my country.

120
00:08:12,707 --> 00:08:17,065
We usually eat packed lunches together.

121
00:08:17,089 --> 00:08:22,555
Japanese university cafeterias have so many menu options.

122
00:08:22,578 --> 00:08:27,212
I get to eat something different every day.

123
00:08:27,235 --> 00:08:32,225
That’s one of my favorite things about it.

124
00:08:32,248 --> 00:08:36,764
Lucky we found a seat!

125
00:08:36,787 --> 00:08:40,968
Yeah, it’s really crowded.

126
00:08:40,992 --> 00:08:44,259
What are you having today?

127
00:08:44,282 --> 00:08:48,670
I went with curry rice.

128
00:08:48,693 --> 00:08:52,593
You like curry rice?

129
00:08:52,616 --> 00:08:56,950
Yeah, I love it.

130
00:08:56,972 --> 00:09:00,641
We have curry in my country too.

131
00:09:00,664 --> 00:09:04,931
But the taste is a little different.

132
00:09:04,954 --> 00:09:08,721
Is Japanese curry sweet?

133
00:09:08,744 --> 00:09:14,293
Yeah, it’s sweet and really smooth.

134
00:09:14,316 --> 00:09:18,227
I’m having udon today.

135
00:09:18,251 --> 00:09:21,394
Udon is delicious too.

136
00:09:21,418 --> 00:09:26,084
Yeah, I love it because it’s warm.

137
00:09:26,107 --> 00:09:28,741
Let’s dig in!

138
00:09:28,764 --> 00:09:31,397
Let’s dig in!

139
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:35,391
The curry is so good!

140
00:09:35,414 --> 00:09:38,081
Glad you like it!

141
00:09:38,104 --> 00:09:40,274
Isn’t it too spicy?

142
00:09:40,297 --> 00:09:43,397
No, it’s fine.

143
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:47,321
I actually love spicy food.

144
00:09:47,345 --> 00:09:50,294
I see.

145
00:09:50,318 --> 00:09:54,493
Is there any Japanese food you don’t like?

146
00:09:54,516 --> 00:09:59,016
Hmm, not yet.

147
00:09:59,039 --> 00:10:01,339
Really?

148
00:10:01,362 --> 00:10:04,736
Can you eat natto?

149
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:10,893
Natto? I’ve never tried it.

150
00:10:10,916 --> 00:10:14,018
You should give it a try sometime.

151
00:10:14,041 --> 00:10:16,575
It’s good!

152
00:10:16,598 --> 00:10:20,572
Okay, I’ll give it a shot!

153
00:10:20,595 --> 00:10:25,383
What's your favorite item on the cafeteria menu?

154
00:10:25,407 --> 00:10:29,242
Curry rice and fried chicken.

155
00:10:29,266 --> 00:10:32,983
Fried chicken is so good, isn't it?

156
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:37,273
Yeah, the meat is so tender.

157
00:10:37,296 --> 00:10:43,030
Oh, by the way, we have a break from university next week.

158
00:10:43,053 --> 00:10:46,619
Really?

159
00:10:46,642 --> 00:10:52,609
Yep, Thursday and Friday are off.

160
00:10:52,632 --> 00:10:55,709
That makes a four-day weekend!

161
00:10:55,732 --> 00:10:59,166
That makes me really happy.

162
00:10:59,189 --> 00:11:04,928
I love the moments when I'm enjoying a warm meal.

163
00:11:04,951 --> 00:11:09,851
Eating and laughing with friends is the best.

164
00:11:09,874 --> 00:11:15,407
Every day of my life is filled with happiness.

165
00:11:15,430 --> 00:11:16,930
Scene 4: Exploring the City on a Sunday

166
00:11:16,930 --> 00:11:20,863
Today is Sunday.

167
00:11:20,886 --> 00:11:26,820
I'm walking around the city alone.

168
00:11:26,843 --> 00:11:32,509
The streets in Japan are bustling on holidays.

169
00:11:32,532 --> 00:11:36,599
There are so many tall buildings.

170
00:11:36,622 --> 00:11:41,922
The buildings here are taller than in my country.

171
00:11:41,945 --> 00:11:49,012
But after walking a bit, you’ll find small parks too.

172
00:11:49,035 --> 00:11:52,309
There are old shops as well.

173
00:11:52,332 --> 00:11:57,091
This city is so fun to explore on foot.

174
00:11:57,115 --> 00:12:00,081
Oh, look at that.

175
00:12:00,104 --> 00:12:02,338
Hmm?

176
00:12:02,361 --> 00:12:07,094
Well, what do you know? What a coincidence!

177
00:12:07,117 --> 00:12:10,755
Hi, Sakura!

178
00:12:10,778 --> 00:12:13,296
Hello!

179
00:12:13,319 --> 00:12:15,898
Taking a walk by yourself?

180
00:12:15,922 --> 00:12:18,355
Yes.

181
00:12:18,378 --> 00:12:22,245
I was walking around taking photos.

182
00:12:22,268 --> 00:12:26,444
Did you get any good shots?

183
00:12:26,467 --> 00:12:28,734
Yes.

184
00:12:28,757 --> 00:12:32,324
I took a picture of the tram.

185
00:12:32,347 --> 00:12:36,453
The trams around here are so cute, aren’t they?

186
00:12:36,476 --> 00:12:38,669
Yes.

187
00:12:38,693 --> 00:12:42,681
We don’t have them in my country.

188
00:12:42,704 --> 00:12:46,438
They move so slowly too.

189
00:12:46,461 --> 00:12:48,598
Yes.

190
00:12:48,621 --> 00:12:52,290
The view from the window is nice as well.

191
00:12:52,314 --> 00:12:56,547
What were you up to, Sakura?

192
00:12:56,570 --> 00:13:00,603
I was out shopping.

193
00:13:00,626 --> 00:13:02,726
Clothes?

194
00:13:02,749 --> 00:13:05,016
Yeah.

195
00:13:05,039 --> 00:13:08,512
I bought a new shirt.

196
00:13:08,536 --> 00:13:11,121
That’s great!

197
00:13:11,145 --> 00:13:13,851
What color is it?

198
00:13:13,874 --> 00:13:18,508
A bright, spring-like color.

199
00:13:18,531 --> 00:13:21,631
I’m sure it’ll look great on you!

200
00:13:21,654 --> 00:13:26,363
I was thinking of grabbing some tea at a café now.

201
00:13:26,386 --> 00:13:28,853
A café?

202
00:13:28,876 --> 00:13:31,749
Want to join me?

203
00:13:31,772 --> 00:13:33,942
Yes.

204
00:13:33,965 --> 00:13:36,798
I’d love to!

205
00:13:36,821 --> 00:13:41,768
There’s a place nearby with delicious cakes.

206
00:13:41,792 --> 00:13:46,164
I love sweets!

207
00:13:46,187 --> 00:13:49,621
Then let’s go there.

208
00:13:49,644 --> 00:13:52,824
Is it a bit far?

209
00:13:52,847 --> 00:13:57,246
It's about a five-minute walk from here.

210
00:13:57,270 --> 00:13:59,938
Got it.

211
00:13:59,961 --> 00:14:05,028
Japanese cakes are so pretty and delicious.

212
00:14:05,051 --> 00:14:07,009
Yes.

213
00:14:07,032 --> 00:14:09,535
I can't wait!

214
00:14:09,558 --> 00:14:14,260
It's always a happy surprise to run into a friend.

215
00:14:14,284 --> 00:14:22,617
Walking alone in the city is fun, but it's even better with someone else.

216
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:27,198
Today is going to be a great day off.

217
00:14:27,221 --> 00:14:28,721
Scene 5: First Tennis Challenge

218
00:14:28,721 --> 00:14:34,467
I joined the university tennis club.

219
00:14:34,491 --> 00:14:39,524
Back in my country, I used to play soccer a lot.

220
00:14:39,547 --> 00:14:42,781
This is my first time playing tennis.

221
00:14:42,804 --> 00:14:47,989
But I wanted to try a new sport.

222
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:52,545
Running on the court feels amazing.

223
00:14:52,568 --> 00:14:56,635
I love the sound of hitting the ball.

224
00:14:56,658 --> 00:15:01,043
I want to get better, so I'll practice a lot.

225
00:15:01,067 --> 00:15:03,972
Good work today!

226
00:15:03,996 --> 00:15:07,177
Good work today.

227
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:10,700
How was practice today?

228
00:15:10,723 --> 00:15:14,037
I'm really tired.

229
00:15:14,061 --> 00:15:17,166
But it was fun.

230
00:15:17,190 --> 00:15:20,726
You've gotten so much better!

231
00:15:20,749 --> 00:15:23,383
Really?

232
00:15:23,406 --> 00:15:26,139
I'm happy to hear that.

233
00:15:26,162 --> 00:15:28,395
Yeah.

234
00:15:28,418 --> 00:15:32,593
At first, I couldn't even hit the ball.

235
00:15:32,617 --> 00:15:35,013
Yes.

236
00:15:35,036 --> 00:15:39,178
Sakura taught me so kindly.

237
00:15:39,202 --> 00:15:43,335
It's because you practice every day.

238
00:15:43,358 --> 00:15:47,728
Tennis is such an interesting sport.

239
00:15:47,752 --> 00:15:50,586
Yeah, it is.

240
00:15:50,609 --> 00:15:53,447
Do you want to enter a match?

241
00:15:53,470 --> 00:15:55,636
Yes.

242
00:15:55,659 --> 00:15:59,759
I'd like to enter a match someday.

243
00:15:59,782 --> 00:16:04,416
There's a small club match next month.

244
00:16:04,439 --> 00:16:07,172
Really?

245
00:16:07,195 --> 00:16:10,666
Could I enter?

246
00:16:10,690 --> 00:16:13,487
Of course!

247
00:16:13,510 --> 00:16:16,288
Want to enter together?

248
00:16:16,312 --> 00:16:18,612
Huh?

249
00:16:18,635 --> 00:16:21,623
As a pair with you, Sakura?

250
00:16:21,647 --> 00:16:24,001
Yeah.

251
00:16:24,024 --> 00:16:28,491
I'll be at the front, and you'll be at the back.

252
00:16:28,514 --> 00:16:30,086
What do you think?

253
00:16:30,109 --> 00:16:34,306
I might hold you back.

254
00:16:34,330 --> 00:16:37,266
It's okay.

255
00:16:37,289 --> 00:16:40,390
The most important thing is to have fun.

256
00:16:40,413 --> 00:16:43,280
Alright.

257
00:16:43,303 --> 00:16:46,012
I'm looking forward to it.

258
00:16:46,035 --> 00:16:51,069
Then let's practice even more starting next week.

259
00:16:51,092 --> 00:16:53,158
Yes.

260
00:16:53,181 --> 00:16:55,548
I'll do my best!

261
00:16:55,571 --> 00:16:59,806
Maybe we should work on running more?

262
00:16:59,829 --> 00:17:02,306
Yeah, I think so.

263
00:17:02,330 --> 00:17:05,469
I'll build up my stamina.

264
00:17:05,493 --> 00:17:09,660
Juice after exercising is so good, isn't it?

265
00:17:09,683 --> 00:17:12,149
Yes.

266
00:17:12,172 --> 00:17:15,239
It's cold and delicious.

267
00:17:15,262 --> 00:17:19,739
I sweated so much.

268
00:17:19,762 --> 00:17:24,077
Make sure you don’t catch a cold.

269
00:17:24,101 --> 00:17:26,067
Yes.

270
00:17:26,090 --> 00:17:28,524
Thank you so much.

271
00:17:28,547 --> 00:17:33,647
I love my club friends so much.

272
00:17:33,670 --> 00:17:37,570
Sweating it out with everyone is the best.

273
00:17:37,593 --> 00:17:43,093
This will be the best memory of my college life in Japan.

274
00:17:43,116 --> 00:17:44,616
Scene 6: My Part-Time Job in Japanese Customer Service

275
00:17:44,616 --> 00:17:51,362
I started a part-time job at a café near the station.

276
00:17:51,385 --> 00:17:57,505
Back in my home country, I’d never worked a part-time job before.

277
00:17:57,529 --> 00:18:02,408
Customer service in Japan is so polite.

278
00:18:02,431 --> 00:18:08,664
At first, I was embarrassed to say 'Irasshaimase!'

279
00:18:08,687 --> 00:18:13,441
But now I can say it in a loud, clear voice.

280
00:18:13,465 --> 00:18:18,244
Seeing customers smile makes me so happy.

281
00:18:18,268 --> 00:18:22,334
Good work today. Your shift over?

282
00:18:22,357 --> 00:18:26,595
Yeah, just finished.

283
00:18:26,619 --> 00:18:30,408
It was really busy today, huh?

284
00:18:30,431 --> 00:18:35,229
Yeah, we had so many customers.

285
00:18:35,253 --> 00:18:38,386
No order mistakes, right?

286
00:18:38,409 --> 00:18:42,709
Nope, not a single one.

287
00:18:42,732 --> 00:18:47,723
Amazing! You’ve really gotten the hang of it.

288
00:18:47,747 --> 00:18:50,980
It’s all thanks to you, Sakura-senpai.

289
00:18:51,003 --> 00:18:54,720
You don’t have to call me 'senpai' here.

290
00:18:54,744 --> 00:18:59,044
No, you’re my senpai at work.

291
00:18:59,067 --> 00:19:01,700
You’re so serious!

292
00:19:01,723 --> 00:19:05,228
Your Japanese has gotten really good, too.

293
00:19:05,251 --> 00:19:09,998
I’ve memorized all the words on the menu.

294
00:19:10,022 --> 00:19:12,455
That’s wonderful!

295
00:19:12,478 --> 00:19:15,978
Have you started talking with customers yet?

296
00:19:16,001 --> 00:19:21,468
Yeah, just a little—like talking about the weather.

297
00:19:21,491 --> 00:19:25,924
Nice! They’ll love that.

298
00:19:25,947 --> 00:19:30,286
I want to get better at making coffee, too.

299
00:19:30,310 --> 00:19:33,810
I’ll teach you someday.

300
00:19:33,833 --> 00:19:36,104
Really?

301
00:19:36,128 --> 00:19:38,901
I'm looking forward to it.

302
00:19:38,924 --> 00:19:42,296
How’s your part-time job in Japan?

303
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:47,221
There’s a lot to learn, but it’s fun.

304
00:19:47,244 --> 00:19:51,399
That’s good to hear.

305
00:19:51,422 --> 00:19:55,889
It feels great to earn my own money.

306
00:19:55,912 --> 00:19:59,179
What are you going to buy with your paycheck?

307
00:19:59,202 --> 00:20:03,548
I want to buy a new camera lens.

308
00:20:03,571 --> 00:20:06,968
Do you have work tomorrow, too?

309
00:20:06,991 --> 00:20:11,100
No, I have the day off.

310
00:20:11,124 --> 00:20:14,243
Make sure to rest up.

311
00:20:14,266 --> 00:20:16,862
Thank you, I will.

312
00:20:16,886 --> 00:20:20,635
Take care on your way home.

313
00:20:20,659 --> 00:20:26,492
The night breeze after work feels so gentle.

314
00:20:26,515 --> 00:20:30,882
I earn my own money by working.

315
00:20:30,905 --> 00:20:35,055
I feel like I’ve grown up a little.

316
00:20:35,078 --> 00:20:36,578
Scene 7: Preparing for an International Student Speech

317
00:20:36,578 --> 00:20:42,489
There’s a speech contest for international students this Saturday.

318
00:20:42,513 --> 00:20:47,146
I was chosen as a representative.

319
00:20:47,169 --> 00:20:50,403
I’m so nervous.

320
00:20:50,426 --> 00:20:55,170
The theme is about my home country and Japan.

321
00:20:55,193 --> 00:20:58,827
I have so much I want to say.

322
00:20:58,850 --> 00:21:04,724
But speaking at length in Japanese is really tough.

323
00:21:04,747 --> 00:21:09,814
Every night, I practice in front of my mirror.

324
00:21:09,837 --> 00:21:13,614
Did you finish your speech draft?

325
00:21:13,638 --> 00:21:17,704
Yes, I wrote something up.

326
00:21:17,727 --> 00:21:20,261
Let me see it.

327
00:21:20,284 --> 00:21:23,517
I’ll check it for you.

328
00:21:23,540 --> 00:21:26,173
Please do.

329
00:21:26,196 --> 00:21:31,371
Wow, this is really good stuff.

330
00:21:31,395 --> 00:21:33,562
Really?

331
00:21:33,585 --> 00:21:37,357
Is any of the Japanese unnatural?

332
00:21:37,380 --> 00:21:42,254
This part sounds a little off.

333
00:21:42,277 --> 00:21:45,577
How should I fix it?

334
00:21:45,600 --> 00:21:50,135
This wording sounds more natural.

335
00:21:50,158 --> 00:21:53,757
Ah, I see. Got it.

336
00:21:53,780 --> 00:21:59,016
You were really moved by Japanese culture, huh?

337
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:04,307
Yes, it’s something we don’t have in my country.

338
00:22:04,330 --> 00:22:08,271
What moved you the most?

339
00:22:08,294 --> 00:22:12,250
How everyone follows the rules.

340
00:22:12,273 --> 00:22:16,407
Oh, like lining up for the train?

341
00:22:16,430 --> 00:22:21,263
Yes! Everyone lines up so neatly.

342
00:22:21,286 --> 00:22:25,953
This will definitely move everyone.

343
00:22:25,976 --> 00:22:28,809
I feel more confident now.

344
00:22:28,832 --> 00:22:31,265
Thank you so much.

345
00:22:31,288 --> 00:22:36,226
All that’s left is to speak up.

346
00:22:36,250 --> 00:22:41,117
Yes, and I want to practice my pronunciation too.

347
00:22:41,139 --> 00:22:45,373
Want to practice a bit now?

348
00:22:45,396 --> 00:22:48,096
Now?

349
00:22:48,119 --> 00:22:51,152
I’m embarrassed...

350
00:22:51,175 --> 00:22:55,119
No one’s here—it’s fine.

351
00:22:55,143 --> 00:22:57,247
Alright.

352
00:22:57,271 --> 00:22:59,771
I’ll read it.

353
00:22:59,794 --> 00:23:03,367
Go ahead. Take your time.

354
00:23:03,390 --> 00:23:06,857
Hello, everyone.

355
00:23:06,880 --> 00:23:10,470
I am...

356
00:23:10,493 --> 00:23:14,200
Nice—your volume is perfect.

357
00:23:14,224 --> 00:23:17,524
I’ll keep this up!

358
00:23:17,547 --> 00:23:20,780
I’ll be there to watch your actual speech.

359
00:23:20,803 --> 00:23:26,348
Just knowing my friends will be listening gives me strength.

360
00:23:26,371 --> 00:23:32,210
I’ll convey my feelings through my words.

361
00:23:32,233 --> 00:23:35,333
I’ll do my absolute best.

362
00:23:35,356 --> 00:23:36,856
Scene 8: Preparing for Final Exams

363
00:23:36,856 --> 00:23:41,627
Final exams are next week.

364
00:23:41,651 --> 00:23:46,884
Tests at Japanese universities are tough.

365
00:23:46,907 --> 00:23:52,607
I study at the library every day.

366
00:23:52,630 --> 00:23:58,497
The view outside the window has turned completely wintry.

367
00:23:58,520 --> 00:24:03,156
We don’t have winter in my country.

368
00:24:03,180 --> 00:24:08,880
So the cold wind is a little hard to handle.

369
00:24:08,903 --> 00:24:14,736
But I think the winter night sky is so beautiful.

370
00:24:14,759 --> 00:24:18,115
How’s your studying going?

371
00:24:18,138 --> 00:24:21,471
Oh, Sakura!

372
00:24:21,494 --> 00:24:25,561
Nope, not at all.

373
00:24:25,584 --> 00:24:29,117
What subject are you studying?

374
00:24:29,140 --> 00:24:32,681
Studying for my economics test.

375
00:24:32,704 --> 00:24:35,684
Economics, huh?

376
00:24:35,708 --> 00:24:39,741
The technical terms are so tough, right?

377
00:24:39,764 --> 00:24:43,834
Yeah. I can't even read some of the kanji.

378
00:24:43,858 --> 00:24:47,098
What part are you stuck on?

379
00:24:47,121 --> 00:24:49,754
I can help explain it.

380
00:24:49,777 --> 00:24:53,744
I don’t get what this graph means.

381
00:24:53,767 --> 00:24:59,045
Oh, this one? See how the numbers are going up?

382
00:24:59,068 --> 00:25:03,181
Yeah, they keep rising.

383
00:25:03,205 --> 00:25:08,471
That means the price is getting higher.

384
00:25:08,494 --> 00:25:12,794
Oh, I see! So that’s what it means.

385
00:25:12,817 --> 00:25:16,117
Exactly! It’s simple, right?

386
00:25:16,140 --> 00:25:20,573
When Sakura explains things, I get it right away.

387
00:25:20,596 --> 00:25:25,375
Glad to hear that! Any other questions?

388
00:25:25,399 --> 00:25:28,699
I’m good for now.

389
00:25:28,722 --> 00:25:31,789
Have you been studying all night?

390
00:25:31,812 --> 00:25:37,112
Yeah, I was up until 3 AM last night.

391
00:25:37,135 --> 00:25:40,640
Don’t push yourself too hard, okay?

392
00:25:40,663 --> 00:25:43,163
No, it’s fine.

393
00:25:43,186 --> 00:25:45,985
I’m young—I’ll be fine!

394
00:25:46,008 --> 00:25:49,761
You’ll get sick if you overdo it.

395
00:25:49,785 --> 00:25:52,940
Okay, I’ll be careful.

396
00:25:52,963 --> 00:25:56,796
Let’s take a little break, then.

397
00:25:56,819 --> 00:26:00,753
Yeah, let’s go buy some coffee.

398
00:26:00,776 --> 00:26:04,746
I’d love some sweet hot cocoa.

399
00:26:04,769 --> 00:26:08,269
I’ll go get it for you.

400
00:26:08,292 --> 00:26:10,859
Really? Are you sure?

401
00:26:10,882 --> 00:26:12,748
Thanks!

402
00:26:12,771 --> 00:26:17,538
You always help me study, so it’s the least I can do.

403
00:26:17,561 --> 00:26:21,028
Well, if you insist!

404
00:26:21,051 --> 00:26:24,284
Just wait a bit, okay?

405
00:26:24,307 --> 00:26:28,045
Winter in Japan is so cold.

406
00:26:28,068 --> 00:26:33,801
But my heart feels warm because of my friends’ kindness.

407
00:26:33,824 --> 00:26:38,537
After exams, I want to go out and have fun with everyone!

408
00:26:38,561 --> 00:26:40,061
Scene 9: Okonomiyaki Stall at the University Festival

409
00:26:40,061 --> 00:26:45,961
Our university festival is this weekend!

410
00:26:45,984 --> 00:26:51,503
Our class is running an okonomiyaki stall.

411
00:26:51,527 --> 00:26:56,960
Okonomiyaki is like Japan’s version of pizza.

412
00:26:56,983 --> 00:27:02,460
I love this food!

413
00:27:02,484 --> 00:27:06,671
We’re decorating our classroom together.

414
00:27:06,694 --> 00:27:11,760
Cutting cardboard, painting—it’s so much fun!

415
00:27:11,783 --> 00:27:17,059
We didn’t have festivals like this back in my country.

416
00:27:17,083 --> 00:27:21,652
Do you think the sign’s colors look good?

417
00:27:21,675 --> 00:27:24,775
It looks really nice!

418
00:27:24,798 --> 00:27:27,698
It really stands out!

419
00:27:27,721 --> 00:27:29,621
Thanks!

420
00:27:29,645 --> 00:27:33,355
You’re so good at drawing!

421
00:27:33,378 --> 00:27:37,812
I’ve loved drawing since I was little.

422
00:27:37,835 --> 00:27:42,701
This character you drew is so cute!

423
00:27:42,724 --> 00:27:45,480
Really?

424
00:27:45,504 --> 00:27:48,378
I'm happy to hear that.

425
00:27:48,402 --> 00:27:52,239
Did you practice making okonomiyaki?

426
00:27:52,263 --> 00:27:54,496
Yes.

427
00:27:54,519 --> 00:27:58,474
I practiced at home yesterday.

428
00:27:58,498 --> 00:28:01,831
Did you flip it well?

429
00:28:01,854 --> 00:28:05,554
I failed the first time.

430
00:28:05,577 --> 00:28:08,644
That's tough, isn't it?

431
00:28:08,667 --> 00:28:12,810
But your second try was perfect.

432
00:28:12,833 --> 00:28:15,405
Amazing!

433
00:28:15,428 --> 00:28:18,062
We're counting on you for the real deal.

434
00:28:18,085 --> 00:28:20,189
Yes.

435
00:28:20,212 --> 00:28:23,045
I'll grill plenty.

436
00:28:23,068 --> 00:28:26,974
Could you help me chop the cabbage too?

437
00:28:26,997 --> 00:28:29,112
Yes.

438
00:28:29,136 --> 00:28:31,836
Leave it to me.

439
00:28:31,859 --> 00:28:37,046
The smell of the sauce is making me hungry.

440
00:28:37,070 --> 00:28:39,020
Yes.

441
00:28:39,044 --> 00:28:41,910
I can't wait to eat!

442
00:28:41,933 --> 00:28:45,567
Tomorrow's gonna be busy.

443
00:28:45,590 --> 00:28:50,323
Hope we get lots of customers.

444
00:28:50,346 --> 00:28:53,820
They'll definitely come in droves.

445
00:28:53,844 --> 00:28:56,877
What if we sell out?

446
00:28:56,900 --> 00:29:01,133
Then we'll celebrate together.

447
00:29:01,156 --> 00:29:04,056
Let's make this a huge success.

448
00:29:04,079 --> 00:29:08,858
Once we're done prepping, let's all go grab a bite.

449
00:29:08,881 --> 00:29:11,415
That’s great!

450
00:29:11,438 --> 00:29:13,938
Let's go!

451
00:29:13,961 --> 00:29:18,894
Preparing for the school festival is so exciting.

452
00:29:18,917 --> 00:29:24,428
Everyone in class is working hard toward the same goal.

453
00:29:24,451 --> 00:29:29,157
I love this sense of unity.

454
00:29:29,181 --> 00:29:30,681
Scene 10: Memories of the School Festival

455
00:29:30,681 --> 00:29:34,114
The school festival is over.

456
00:29:34,137 --> 00:29:38,970
Our stall was a huge success.

457
00:29:38,994 --> 00:29:43,584
We sold out of all the okonomiyaki.

458
00:29:43,608 --> 00:29:49,574
The campus is so quiet after all the cleanup.

459
00:29:49,597 --> 00:29:55,131
It feels a little lonely after the festival.

460
00:29:55,154 --> 00:30:01,705
But the fun memories will stay with us forever.

461
00:30:01,728 --> 00:30:04,261
Good work today!

462
00:30:04,284 --> 00:30:09,384
Oh, Sakura. You must be tired.

463
00:30:09,407 --> 00:30:12,960
It was an incredible festival, wasn't it?

464
00:30:12,984 --> 00:30:17,084
Yes, it was the best day ever.

465
00:30:17,107 --> 00:30:21,015
Thanks for grilling all day.

466
00:30:21,039 --> 00:30:25,772
No, I had so much fun.

467
00:30:25,795 --> 00:30:30,228
Customers said it was delicious.

468
00:30:30,251 --> 00:30:34,918
That makes me so happy to hear.

469
00:30:34,941 --> 00:30:38,925
Everyone in class was thrilled too.

470
00:30:38,948 --> 00:30:41,943
It really turned out great.

471
00:30:41,967 --> 00:30:45,067
I'm a little worn out.

472
00:30:45,090 --> 00:30:49,356
Yeah, my feet are killing me.

473
00:30:49,379 --> 00:30:52,279
Make sure to rest up.

474
00:30:52,302 --> 00:30:56,436
Sakura, make sure you get some rest too.

475
00:30:56,459 --> 00:30:59,592
What are you doing next?

476
00:30:59,615 --> 00:31:03,082
I'm going out with friends to celebrate.

477
00:31:03,104 --> 00:31:06,838
Oh, I'll join you.

478
00:31:06,861 --> 00:31:09,407
Same place?

479
00:31:09,430 --> 00:31:12,730
The izakaya by the station.

480
00:31:12,753 --> 00:31:16,087
Oh, same here.

481
00:31:16,110 --> 00:31:19,585
Then let's go together.

482
00:31:19,608 --> 00:31:23,541
Sure, let's walk there.

483
00:31:23,564 --> 00:31:27,156
Let's eat a lot today.

484
00:31:27,180 --> 00:31:31,313
Yeah, and drink plenty too!

485
00:31:31,336 --> 00:31:35,203
I really had the best time today.

486
00:31:35,226 --> 00:31:37,897
Same here.

487
00:31:37,920 --> 00:31:41,153
It's a memory I'll never forget.

488
00:31:41,176 --> 00:31:44,758
See you at school tomorrow.

489
00:31:44,782 --> 00:31:48,449
Yes, see you tomorrow.

490
00:31:48,472 --> 00:31:53,306
The night sky is adorned with a beautiful moon.

491
00:31:53,330 --> 00:31:57,996
It's the same moon I see from my country.

492
00:31:58,019 --> 00:32:04,553
I'm spending irreplaceable time in this country.

493
00:32:04,576 --> 00:32:10,117
Tomorrow is sure to be another wonderful day.